course: dictionary
lesson: 9095
title: Thick, runny mixtures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from farms and science, and the words around them can help you work out what they mean. «Farmers spread manure and slurry, a runny mix of muck and water, on fields as fertiliser.» The words after slurry tell you what it is.
explain: Slurry is a thick, runny mixture of water and something solid, such as mud, cement or crushed rock. On farms, slurry is liquid animal manure kept in tanks or pits until it is spread on fields to help crops grow. Try your meaning in the sentence: spread a runny mix of muck and water on fields. It still makes sense.
explain: Scientists use slurry as an example of a mixture. The solid bits float about in the liquid, and if you leave it, they settle at the bottom. A slurry is not a solution, because the solid bits stay separate from the water.
explain: Slurry pits and tanks are very dangerous. They give off poisonous gases, and people and animals can drown in them. «Farms have dangers such as tractors, bulls, cows with calves and deep slurry pits.» Always keep away from them, and tell an adult if you see one.
fact: Slurry is a thick, runny mixture of water and something solid, such as mud, cement or crushed rock.
fact: On a farm, slurry is liquid animal manure, made of dung and urine mixed with water.
fact: Farmers keep slurry in tanks or pits, then spread it on fields as fertiliser.
fact: In science, slurry is a mixture and not a solution: the solid bits settle if you leave it.
fact: Slurry pits and tanks are dangerous because they give off poisonous gases, so always keep away.
exercise: «Farmers spread manure and slurry, a runny mix of muck and water, on fields.» What is slurry? | *A runny mix of muck and water | A dry, hard lump of soil | A kind of farm tractor | A type of tall grass
exercise: «Farms have dangers such as tractors, bulls, cows with calves and deep slurry pits.» Which word tells you where slurry is kept? | *pits | tractors | bulls | calves
exercise: In science, what happens to the solid bits in a slurry if you leave it? | They float up and turn into a gas | They dissolve and disappear | They turn into solid rock straight away | *They settle at the bottom
test: Slurry is best described as: | *a thick, runny mixture of water and something solid | a kind of gas | a hard, dry rock | a type of sweet
test: Why must children keep away from slurry pits? | They smell of flowers | *They give off poisonous gases and people can drown in them | They are too shallow to see | They are full of fish
exam: Why is a slurry pit dangerous? | It is too small to fall into | *It gives off poisonous gases and people can drown in it | It is full of cold, clean water | It is only a puddle after rain
